      "description": "15 cards: 5 traditional foil commons, 4 traditional foil uncommons, a borderless celestial basic land (traditional foil 66.6% or galaxy foil 33.3%), a traditional foil rare (86%) or mythic rare (14%), a Commander card (a borderless mythic rare 9% or an extended-art rare 91%), a Booster Fun card (extended-art rare 47%, mythic rare 5%; viewport land rare 7%, mythic rare 4%; triumphant rare 17%, mythic rare 3%; surreal space rare 15%, mythic rare 2%), a Stellar Sights land (rare 36%, mythic rare 9%; poster rare 18%, mythic rare 4%; traditional foil rare 12%, mythic rare 3%; traditional foil poster rare 6%, mythic rare 1.5%; galaxy foil rare 6%, mythic rare 1.5%; galaxy foil poster rare 3% or mythic rare) and a foil Booster Fun card (traditional foil extended-art rare 38%, mythic rare 4%; viewport land rare 6%, mythic rare 3%; triumphant rare 13%, mythic rare 2%; surreal space rare 12%, mythic rare 2%; a Special Guests card 6%; a Japan showcase card 9% or in fracture foil 1%; galaxy foil viewport land rare 2%, mythic rare 1%; or the singularity foil headliner). Published only as less than 1%, so derived: the galaxy foil poster mythic rare is 0.75% (half a rare's per-card odds, as in the other Stellar Sights land treatments), and the singularity foil headliner is 0.2%, a galaxy foil mythic rare viewport land's per-card odds. The published odds of the Stellar Sights land slot add up to slightly over 100% after rounding, so they are used as relative weights. Galaxy, singularity and fracture foils are shown as traditional foils except fracture foil, which has its own printing. Each booster also holds a traditional foil double-sided token or an art card, which aren't game cards.",
